From c0629a03a3e1068ad62bfad1b0b8070d7651a9d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craig Shaw <craig@craigshaw.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 18:14:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Resume timed table scans with proven guest stack saves

Allow scheduler continuation entries at statically proven local stack depths and reconstruct their owning entry stack. Add bounded word stack, indexed table-read, local JMP and register-transfer timing support. Preserve high-byte-first saves and word DEC writes, materialize long indirect pointers once, and test word ORA bank carry and crossing cycles.

Synthetic coverage includes 104 complete comparisons and 704 event comparisons, including interpreted entry, nested saves, compiled and interpreted callees, and RTS/RTL returns. Python v2 and shared C suites pass. Unselected generation is unchanged.

Co-authored-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>
